<Wiki
  title="puv init"
  description="Start a puv project in the current directory, or create a named directory and start it there."
>
  <p class="kicker">Wiki</p>
  <h1>init</h1>
  <p>
    <code>puv init</code> starts a project and writes <code>puv.toml</code>. The PHP patch is
    recorded by the next command, <a href="/wiki/commands/use"><code>puv use</code></a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Current directory</h2>
  <pre class="block">mkdir my-tool
cd my-tool
puv init</pre>
  <p>
    Use this when the directory already exists and is empty. The walk that follows is a
    <a href="/wiki/new-project">new project</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Create the directory</h2>
  <pre class="block">puv init my-app
cd my-app</pre>
  <p>
    The argument is the directory name. puv creates it, then writes the manifest inside it.
  </p>

  <h2>What you have afterwards</h2>
  <p>
    A <code>puv.toml</code> with a <code>[project]</code> table. Packages, scripts, and the
    package format are added later. The full shape is on <a href="/wiki/files">files</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    A directory that already contains <code>composer.json</code> should use
    <a href="/wiki/commands/contain"><code>puv contain</code></a>, not <code>init</code>. An
    application skeleton should use <a href="/wiki/commands/create"><code>puv create</code></a>.
  </p>
</Wiki>
